When you find a SQL injection, one way attack you can do is through utilizing "xp_cmdshell, which is a stored procedure in Microsoft SQL Server that allows command and programs to be executed within the server."
Check if code execution is working without errors using xp_cmdshell
' UNION SELECT NULL, NULL; EXEC xp_cmdshell 'cmd /c whoami' --
if there was no error, then the xp_cmdshell should be running it correctly. Craft a reverse shell over 443.
